# Cloudflare Workers static-asset response headers (applies to every file).
# Conservative on purpose: nothing here restricts scripts/styles (the pages use inline code), it only closes
# the doors this site never needs -- being framed by other sites, plugin content, <base> hijacking, MIME sniffing.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'

# Third-party bundles and icons never change without a file rename/bump, so let browsers keep them for a week
# instead of revalidating on every page. (HTML, own JS/CSS and sw.js keep the default revalidate-every-time.)
/js/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
# Vendor scripts are referenced as ...js?v=N in the pages: when you swap in a new version of a library, bump N in the
# <script> tags (search for "?v=") and every visitor fetches the new file immediately instead of after the week is up.
